golden-judge-2.summary:
I judged all 41 Today goldens in e92266bd against the 42510757 masters: 36 right, 5 unsure, 0 wrong. Across the glance states the regeneration does three things:
- removes the muddy olive rim light on Day hero cards;
- removes the lime glow under Night hero cards;
- turns the volt-filled study-day checks (and the lime chevron on the lead-in cue) neutral.

That leaves the hero key and the A1 Start key as the only volt fills. The one real redesign is the alternatives (Something else) sheet. It drops the Start-twin layout (Quick practice hero tile with a volt play button, nested tile grid) for four list rows, each with a reason. That fixes the critic's item. I found no clipping, overlap, second Mobi or broken layout at 360 dp, 412 dp or 130% text.

Unsure:
- **today_sealed (Day and Night):** the duplicated Road to May cue sits on screen with the road heading, Quick 10 wraps with 10 orphaned, and Open results directly is plain text.
- **today_why_sheet (Day and Night):** about 35 lime correct-answer dots remain, inconsistent with the now-neutral week checks.

Leftover lime marks the commit did not address, carried over unchanged rather than regressions:
- the road pips, the May flag line and the +33 on Mock 6 text;
- the Night resume progress fill;
- the Night See why underline on the sparse state;
- the lime ring on the Revise icon in the alternatives sheet.

I worked read-only in wt-v13, and my temp folder is deleted.

golden-judge-4.summary:
Golden judge 4 (practice): I judged all 34 files that e92266bd changed under flutter_app/test/golden/practice/goldens, each against its 42510757 master. Result: 26 right, 6 wrong, 2 unsure.

Right (26). The Practice tab masters change in a consistent, intended way:
- the 'Up next in ...' eyebrow is removed;
- the muddy olive Day rim on the hero cards is gone (critic item);
- the hero's volt 'Start 10 questions' / 'Resume' becomes a glass or outlined secondary key, so the page carries no volt fill next to the bar's Start key (suggestion_card.dart, line 211);
- the Quick practice and By chapter tiles lose the lime bolt and green glow and gain grain texture and a warm lamp (the textured cards are kept; the Economics resume card keeps its teal light);
- tiles are equal height.

The confirm and chapter-picker sheet masters only changed in the backdrop strip above the sheet (diff box y < 181), so the sheets themselves are identical. In confirm_chapter_credits the second volt fill that showed above the sheet is gone. The closing frames lose the olive rim.

Wrong (6): all six quick_start_deck masters (day, night, pressed, resume). Their own changes are fine: the olive rim is removed and the bolt halo is smaller. But each master still shows two volt fills: the play disc plus the solid lime 'Repair the next mistake' check disc. They also keep the lime hero bolt. In the resume variant the NTA title sits about 40 dp below the Repair title in the same row. All of this was already in the old masters, not introduced by this commit, but accepting these masters would lock it in.

Unsure (2): tab_offline day and night. The disabled Start key now differs from the enabled secondary key only by dimmer text; the old one had a grey fill. The offline reason line is still cut off with an ellipsis.

Lime marks that remain in masters I marked right (follow-ups, not regressions):
- the lime ring on Smart practice;
- the lime bookmark on By chapter;
- the lime dot meter and the 'Free today' lime tick in the confirm sheets;
- the lime Balanced dot.

I wrote the old masters to a temp folder in my scratchpad (judge4old) and deleted it at the end. Nothing in wt-v13 was edited, committed or run.
